{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DESIGN.md | sed -n '1,235p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# True Base Bench — design brief (v1)\n     2\t\n     3\t**True Base Bench, by Anima Labs.** This file is the single design source for the site. If it conflicts with `docs/SPEC.md`, SPEC.md wins for *what* is measured and shipped; this file wins for *how it looks, moves and reads*. Change this file before you build something that departs from it.\n     4\t\n     5\t---\n     6\t\n     7\t## 0. Decision\n     8\t\n     9\tTwo directions were proposed: **A, \"Monograph\"** (a typeset research report with scroll-driven explainers and provenance shown as citations) and **B, \"Strip Chart\"** (an observatory instrument with the leaderboard first, plates with a transport bar, and every mark to scale).\n    10\t\n    11\t**Winner: B, \"Strip Chart\".** Grafts from A are listed below.\n    12\t\n    13\tWhy B wins:\n    14\t- **Leaderboard as the product.** A researcher citing the bench lands on the readings. B's ladder strip, its Ranked/Ladders views and its raw-feature-on-ramp cells are the densest legible presentation in either brief.\n    15\t- **Explainers grounded in v1 data.** B draws its explainers from fields that already exist. Plate A uses a distribution constructed so that its H equals `F_H` and its s equals `F_CE`. The teacher-forcing histogram fills to the real `selfboot.reliability.bins` counts. The surname dot field thins to the real `exp(H)`. The run tape fills to the real `X_runfrac_wiki`. A's explainers (a) and (b) mostly fall back to unlabelled schematics until new bundle fixtures exist.\n    16\t- **Honest axes.** For the gap range of +0.016 to −0.917, B's linked lens panel is more honest than A's piecewise axis with a break. SPEC asks for charts to scale.\n    17\t- **Feasibility.** A plate with discrete steps and a transport bar is far easier to build and test in Vite + TS than sticky scrollytelling. It also works at 400px without a 48vh sticky figure fighting the scroll.\n    18\t\n    19\tGrafted from A:\n    20\t1. **Visible provenance.** Every live number is a `<Num>` with a dotted underline. Hover or focus pops out its exact bundle path and raw value. Every plate ends with a `Source:` line. A's \"nothing is hardcoded, and you can see it\" device becomes the house signature.\n    21\t2. **The margin column.** On reading pages at ≥1100px there is a 280px margin for sidenotes, narrow captions and provenance pop-outs, and step text in the explainers.\n    22\t3. **Stepped states over a free timeline.** Explainers are lists of discrete states. Every step has a paragraph of prose with `<Num>`s, and all step paragraphs stay readable without motion.\n    23\t4. **Pedagogical beats.** Entropy as a *balance point* (the fulcrum). Bars dropping onto the surprisal axis. The counter reset and the too-short streak in the run rule. The ball settling onto the ramp. \"Same overall, different reasons\".\n    24\t5. **Computed specimens.** Every default model or pair in an explainer is chosen by a rule over the bundle, never by a hardcoded id (§6.4).\n    25\t6. **Programmatic checks on findings.** Every finding claim has a check. If a future bundle breaks it, a visible **Data note** appears. A claim is never silently left standing.\n    26\t7. **Model-page details.** A default \"compare\" sibling, the arithmetic line, an \"Explained in Methodology §n\" link on every section, and the full fingerprint grouped by prefix.\n    27\t8. **Surname frames as real text.** Prompt cards show the actual frame strings from `SURNAME_PROMPTS` in `docs/vh_score.py`, and a test keeps them in sync. They are not paraphrases.\n    28\t9. **Colophon.** The footer prints the bundle provenance: file, schema_version, generated, n_models, n_families.\n    29\t\n    30\tRejected from A: scroll-triggered sticky scrollytelling, the progressively filled circle glyphs (a half-filled circle is unreadable at 7px and clashes with \"hollow = comparison\"), and the piecewise axis. Rejected from B: ±0.02 hardcoded as the band (it is computed now, see §6.4), and the paraphrased surname frame.\n    31\t\n    32\t---\n    33\t\n    34\t## 1. Principles\n    35\t\n    36\t1. **An instrument, not a pitch.** No hero, no gradient, no glass, no illustration, no emoji. Nothing is centred: text is left-aligned and numbers are right-aligned in tables.\n    37\t2. **Every number points to its source.** Any numeral rendered from data is a `<Num>` that knows its bundle path. Prose never contains a typed measurement. Method constants (ramp anchors, run length 16, H < 0.2, Census reference values) come from `src/method.ts` or `reference.*`, are labelled \"definition\", and are covered by tests (§12).\n    38\t3. **To scale or labelled.** Scales are linear unless an axis label says otherwise. A log axis is allowed only with labelled decade ticks and the word \"log\" in the axis title. There are no broken axes. Extreme ranges use a lens panel.\n    39\t4. **Colour carries one variable.** Training stage only, always paired with a glyph and a text code. Score bars are monochrome. Diverging values use direction plus the U+2212 sign, never red/green.\n    40\t5. **Motion only depicts a process from the measurement.** The leaderboard and the model page animate only state changes.\n    41\t6. **Illustrations say so.** Any element whose *shape* is constructed or schematic (plate A's distribution, plate D's run arrangement, C1's simulated draws) carries a visible label, either `constructed` or `schematic`. It prints no number that does not come from the bundle or `method.ts`.\n    42\t7. **\"Higher is not better\".** The score measures distance from a pre-anneal base. Copy and the column header must say so. 1 = indistinguishable from a pre-anneal checkpoint.\n    43\t\n    44\t---\n    45\t\n    46\t## 2. Identity tokens\n    47\t\n    48\t### 2.1 Palette\n    49\t\n    50\tTokens are defined on `:root`. The dark set is defined under `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)`, guarded by `:root:not([data-theme=\"light\"])`, and again under `:root[data-theme=\"dark\"]`. `body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); }` is set explicitly. Charts read every colour from tokens, so the dark theme needs no chart code.\n    51\t\n    52\t```css\n    53\t:root {\n    54\t  /* paper */\n    55\t  --bg: #F5F3EE;          /* page */\n    56\t  --bg-plate: #ECE8DF;    /* figure plates, explainer bands */\n    57\t  --bg-raised: #FBFAF7;   /* sticky thead, tooltips, menus, prompt cards */\n    58\t  --ink: #1A1D21;         /* 15.3:1 on bg */\n    59\t  --ink-2: #4A4F57;       /* secondary text, 7.4:1 */\n    60\t  --ink-3: #5F646C;       /* ticks, captions, source lines; 5.4:1 bg, 4.9:1 plate */\n    61\t  --rule: #D8D2C4;        /* hairlines, gridlines (decorative) */\n    62\t  --rule-strong: #B9B1A0; /* axis lines, null hatch (decorative only, 1.9:1) */\n    63\t  --control: #5F646C;     /* form-control borders, must meet 3:1 */\n    64\t  --track: #E3DED3;       /* empty bar track */\n    65\t  --bar: #2A2E35;         /* score bar fill, monochrome */\n    66\t  --hl: #F3DD86;          /* highlighter: token/row/rung under study; text on it is --ink only */\n    67\t  --focus: #0B5CAD;       /* 2px ring, 2px offset; 6.0:1 */\n    68\t  --link: #0B5CAD;\n    69\t  --zero: #4A4F57;        /* zero lines, 1px (1.5px on gap axes) */\n    70\t  --band: rgba(30,122,106,0.12); /* pre-anneal band on gap axes */\n    71\t  /* stage — marks only, never text */\n    72\t  --st-pre:  #1E7A6A;  /* verdigris, 4.7:1 */\n    73\t  --st-anl:  #A86B00;  /* ochre, 4.0:1 */\n    74\t  --st-base: #3B5B9A;  /* slate blue, 6.0:1 */\n    75\t  --st-post: #B23A26;  /* brick, 5.4:1 */\n    76\t}\n    77\t/* night slate (not pure black) */\n    78\t--bg #111417; --bg-plate #181C20; --bg-raised #1E2328;\n    79\t--ink #E8E4DA; --ink-2 #B5B0A5; --ink-3 #8C887F (5.2:1);\n    80\t--rule #2C3238; --rule-strong #434B53; --control #8C887F; --track #262C31; --bar #DCD7CB;\n    81\t--hl #5C4E14; --focus #7FB2FF; --link #7FB2FF; --zero #B5B0A5;\n    82\t--band: rgba(79,191,168,0.14);\n    83\t--st-pre #4FBFA8; --st-anl #E0A63A; --st-base #8EA8E8; --st-post #F07C62;  /* all ≥ 6.8:1 */\n    84\t```\n    85\t\n    86\tWhy these stage colours rather than an ordinal ramp: 26 of the 32 v1 checkpoints are `base` or `post-trained`. Slate blue against brick stays far apart (ΔE ≥ 66) under deuteranopia, protanopia and tritanopia simulation. Stage order is already carried by position (strip rows, ladder order). Anneal (ochre) against post (brick) is the weakest pair under deuteranopia (ΔE 16), so shape always backs it.\n    87\t\n    88\tText on `--hl` is always `--ink` (in dark mode `--ink-3` on `--hl` fails). Stage colours are never used for text.\n    89\t\n    90\t### 2.2 Stage glyphs (redundant encoding)\n    91\t\n    92\t| stage | glyph | code |\n    93\t|---|---|---|\n    94\t| pre-anneal | filled circle | PRE |\n    95\t| anneal | filled diamond | ANL |\n    96\t| base | filled square | BASE |\n    97\t| post-trained | filled triangle (apex up) | POST |\n    98\t\n    99\t- A **hollow** glyph (1.5px stroke, same colour) means a *comparison or ghost*: a sibling, a compare model, or specimen B against A.\n   100\t- Size is 8px in tables, 7px in charts, and 10px in legends and titles. A single `<Glyph stage hollow size>` SVG component draws all of them.\n   101\t- An inline legend row (glyph, code and name) appears wherever stage colour appears on a page. The stage name is also always available in text: a table column, an aria-label or a tooltip.\n   102\t\n   103\t### 2.3 Wordmark and icon\n   104\t\n   105\t- The wordmark is \"True Base Bench\" in Source Serif 4, 600, 18px, preceded by a 16px **ramp glyph**: an SVG polyline drawn flat, then slope, then flat, which is the clipped linear ramp. The stroke is 1.5px `--ink`.\n   106\t- The same glyph, on a transparent background, is the favicon (`favicon.svg`, with a `prefers-color-scheme` style inside).\n   107\t- A hairline separates the wordmark from \"by Anima Labs\", set in Plex Sans Condensed 12px `--ink-2` and linking to https://github.com/anima-research. The footer repeats it. There is no other branding.\n   108\t\n   109\t### 2.4 Other tokens\n   110\t\n   111\t```\n   112\t--radius: 2px            (controls only; plates, tables and bars are 0)\n   113\t--hair: 1px\n   114\t--space: 4 8 12 16 24 32 48 64\n   115\t--dur-1: 120ms  (hover, focus, UI)\n   116\t--dur-2: 180ms  (FLIP row reorder, disclosure)\n   117\t--dur-step: 160ms (one token step in explainers)\n   118\t--dur-3: 600ms  (explainer state tween)\n   119\t--ease-settle: cubic-bezier(.2,0,0,1)   (marks settling)\n   120\t--ease-inout: cubic-bezier(.65,0,.35,1) (state tweens)\n   121\tlinear for cursors and tapes\n   122\t```\n   123\t\n   124\tThere are no shadows, gradients or icons, except the stage glyphs, the ramp glyph, a 12px disclosure chevron, the sort triangle and the transport icons (play, pause, step back, step forward, replay, drawn as simple SVG).\n   125\t\n   126\t---\n   127\t\n   128\t## 3. Type\n   129\t\n   130\tAll fonts are self-hosted through **Fontsource** npm packages (exact pinned versions, latin subset, `font-display: swap`) and bundled by Vite. There is no runtime font CDN. Preload only Plex Sans Condensed 400 and Source Serif 4 (variable). The total budget is 7 files.\n   131\t\n   132\t| family | use | fallback |\n   133\t|---|---|---|\n   134\t| **Source Serif 4** (variable, opsz; 400, 400 italic, 600) | page titles, finding headlines, prose, step text, wordmark | \"Iowan Old Style\", Georgia, serif |\n   135\t| **IBM Plex Sans Condensed** (400, 500, 600) | all UI: tables, nav, ticks, labels, buttons, captions | \"Arial Narrow\", \"Roboto Condensed\", system-ui, sans-serif (with a `size-adjust` fallback face to limit layout shift) |\n   136\t| **IBM Plex Mono** (400, 500) | field paths, model ids, source lines, prompt cards, code, bundle stamp | ui-monospace, \"SF Mono\", Menlo, Consolas, monospace |\n   137\t\n   138\tPlex Sans Condensed always sets `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums`. Serif numerals inside prose `<Num>` also switch to tabular lining figures.\n   139\t\n   140\tScale (px/line-height):\n   141\t\n   142\t| size | use |\n   143\t|---|---|\n   144\t| 11/14 | ticks, source lines (mono), plate labels |\n   145\t| 12/16 | captions, table line 2 |\n   146\t| 13/18 | table body (desktop) |\n   147\t| 14/20 | UI, phone table, margin notes |\n   148\t| 17/27 | serif prose, max 64ch (16/26 under 720px) |\n   149\t| 20/28 | lede, finding standfirst (serif italic) |\n   150\t| 26/32 | h2, finding headlines (serif 600) |\n   151\t| 34/40 | h1 and the overall score on the model page |\n   152\t\n   153\t- **Plate labels** are Plex Sans Condensed 500, 11px, uppercase, letter-spacing 0.08em, `--ink-3`, for example `PLATE C2 · CALIBRATION GAP ALONG THE OLMO-2 LADDER`. Finding kickers use the same style (`F1`), and so do section kickers on reading pages (`§3`).\n   154\t\n   155\t### 3.1 Number formatting (`src/lib/numfmt.ts`, the only formatter)\n   156\t\n   157\t| kind | format | example |\n   158\t|---|---|---|\n   159\t| overall and sub-scores | 3 decimals | 0.983 |\n   160\t| gaps, nats, signed quantities | signed, 3 decimals, U+2212 minus, unit in `--ink-3` | −0.917 nats, +0.016 |\n   161\t| unsigned nats (H, CE, KL) | 2 decimals for KL, 3 for H/CE | KL 2.55; H 1.865 nats |\n   162\t| shares and rates | percent, 1 decimal; 2 decimals below 1% | 10.2%, 0.19% |\n   163\t| ratios | ×1.9 |\n   164\t| counts | thin-space (U+2009) thousands | 1 356 458 |\n   165\t| exp(H) \"effective names\" | integer with ≈ | ≈ 757 |\n   166\t| rank ties | \"=\" prefix, ties judged on the *displayed* 3-decimal value | =29 |\n   167\t| null | \"—\" with `title=\"not measured for this checkpoint\"` |\n   168\t\n   169\t---\n   170\t\n   171\t## 4. Layout\n   172\t\n   173\t### 4.1 Grid\n   174\t\n   175\tThe container has max-width 1280px and is centred in the viewport. Content inside it is left-aligned. Side gutters are 16px under 720px, 24px from 720 to 1099px, and 32px from 1100px up.\n   176\t\n   177\tReading pages (Model, Methodology, Findings, Measure) at ≥1100px use named tracks:\n   178\t\n   179\t```\n   180\t[rail 176px] 40px [main 640px] 48px [margin 280px]\n   181\t```\n   182\t\n   183\t- **rail**: a sticky in-page index (model sections, explainer list, F1–F6, measure steps). The current item has a 2px `--ink` left rule. It is hidden under 1100px and replaced by a horizontal scroll-snapped chip row under the page title.\n   184\t- **main**: prose, at most 64ch.\n   185\t- **margin**: sidenotes, narrow captions, `<Num>` provenance pop-outs, definitions and explainer step text.\n   186\t- **wide** = main + gap + margin (968px), used for plates. Full-bleed is never used.\n   187\t- From 720 to 1099px, margin notes become inline asides: 14px Plex Sans Condensed `--ink-2`, with a 2px `--rule-strong` left border and a 12px indent.\n   188\t- Under 720px there is a single column.\n   189\t\n   190\tThe Leaderboard uses the full container width with a 12-column, 24px-gutter grid.\n   191\t\n   192\t### 4.2 Chrome\n   193\t\n   194\t- **Top bar** (48px, sticky, `--bg` with a 1px `--rule` bottom border). On the left: the wordmark and \"by Anima Labs\". Then the nav: Leaderboard · Findings · Methodology · Measure your model. Nav items are plain 14px links; the current page has a 2px `--ink` underline, with no pills. On the right: the **bundle stamp** in mono 11px, `bench_v1 · 2026-10-13 · 32 models` (from the manifest/bundle `schema_version`, `generated` and `n_models`), and a 3-state theme switch (System / Light / Dark).\n   195\t- Under 720px the nav collapses into a disclosure button labelled \"Menu\". The stamp moves to the footer.\n   196\t- **Footer (colophon)**: \"True Base Bench by Anima Labs\" with a GitHub link · bundle file name · schema_version · generated · n_models · n_families (all read from the bundle) · \"Download bundle (JSON)\" · \"Data: OVH Object Storage, manifest.json\" · theme switch · **Reduce motion** toggle.\n   197\t- Both the theme and the reduce-motion setting live in `localStorage` with every access in try/catch. The page renders correctly with storage unavailable.\n   198\t\n   199\t### 4.3 Plates\n   200\t\n   201\tA **Plate** has a `--bg-plate` background, a 1px `--rule` top border, 0 radius, and 20px padding (12px on phones). It contains:\n   202\t1. a plate label (`PLATE C2 · …`);\n   203\t2. the figure (SVG, `role=\"img\"`, and an `aria-label` sentence generated from the data);\n   204\t3. a caption (12/16 Plex Sans Condensed `--ink-2`), which goes in the margin column for narrow figures;\n   205\t4. a **SourceLine** in mono 11px `--ink-3`: `Source: bench_v1.json · models[*].fingerprint.F_calib_gap` (one path per line if there are several);\n   206\t5. a **\"Data\" disclosure** that reveals the plotted numbers as a real `<table>`. This is also the text alternative.\n   207\t\n   208\t---\n   209\t\n   210\t## 5. Components (shared kit, `src/components/`)\n   211\t\n   212\t| component | contract |\n   213\t|---|---|\n   214\t| `Num` | `<Num path=\"models[id].fingerprint.F_calib_gap\" fmt=\"gap\" />`. It renders the formatted value with a 1px dotted `--ink-3` underline. It is focusable (tabindex 0). On hover or focus it shows a pop-out: in the margin column on desktop, otherwise as a tooltip. The pop-out reads `models[olmo2-7b_instruct].fingerprint.F_calib_gap = −0.91682` (raw value to 5 significant figures). A null renders as \"—\". This is the **only** way prose shows a measurement. |\n   215\t| `SourceLine` | the field paths a figure reads |\n   216\t| `Glyph` | stage, hollow, size |\n   217\t| `StageLegend` | one inline row of glyph, code and name for each stage present |\n   218\t| `Axis`, `Track`, `Bar` | linear by default. Ticks are 11px `--ink-3`, gridlines 1px `--rule`, the axis line `--rule-strong`. The axis title always states the quantity and unit (`calibration gap, mean(H − s), nats`). |\n   219\t| `DivergingBar` | grows from a 1px `--zero` line in `--bar`, with the sign in the label |\n   220\t| `RampCell` | the raw feature drawn on its ramp's own axis: the track is shaded `--band` from the 1-anchor outward, a tick marks the 0-anchor, and the value is a 2px `--ink` tick |\n   221\t| `LensPanel` | a main linear axis plus a second linear axis below it for a sub-range, joined by 1px `--rule-strong` connector lines from the sub-range ends. Both are labelled. |\n   222\t| `NullPlate` | a 45° `--rule-strong` hatch with one sentence, for example \"Surname test not run for this checkpoint.\" |\n   223\t| `Tooltip` | `--bg-raised`, 1px `--rule`, 0 radius. It shows label, value and field path. It is reachable by keyboard because marks are focusable; arrow keys move between marks within a chart, and Esc closes the tooltip. |\n   224\t| `Transport` | Play/Pause · Step back · Step forward · Replay · `step k of n`. Each control is a `<button>` with an aria-label. When the plate has focus, Space toggles play and the arrow keys step. |\n   225\t| `ModelPicker` | a segmented control for the computed defaults plus an \"any model…\" combobox (type-ahead over label, family and id) |\n   226\t| `CopyButton` | copies an id, a code block or JSON, and confirms through `aria-live` |\n   227\t\n   228\tCharts are hand-written SVG with pinned `d3-scale`, `d3-shape` and `d3-array`, bundled. No charting library is used. The 1 000-cell tapes and the ~1 022-dot field are SVG as well. Canvas is allowed only if profiling on a mid-range phone shows frames longer than 16ms; in that case the SVG Data table remains the accessible path.\n   229\t\n   230\t---\n   231\t\n   232\t## 6. Data layer\n   233\t\n   234\t### 6.1 Loading\n   235\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
