{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"agent_message","text":"The site’s claim checks miss some of the claims they appear to validate. The surname check tests top-10 concentration, not whether a model reproduces the Census ranking; the domain check ignores positive gaps above +0.02. I also confirmed that runtime validation accepts malformed data, and found a mobile accessibility defect: the visible replacement sub-scores are hidden from assistive technology.\n"}}
